# Production builds are SAME-ORIGIN: nginx proxies /api, /auth, /sse to the
# backend on the deployed domain (beta, prod), so the frontend must NOT target a
# fixed host. An empty VITE_API_URL makes every `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL ?? …`
# resolve to "" (relative, same-origin) instead of the dev fallback
# http://localhost:8000 — which would otherwise send login/auth/mutations to the
# user's own machine. The SAME CI artifact ships to all domains, so "" is the only
# correct value. `vite build` loads this file (production mode); `vite dev` does
# not, so local dev keeps its localhost:8000 defaults + the /api proxy.
VITE_API_URL=
